  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Abdullah Hisamuddin Khan vs The State Of Maharashtra on 18 February, 2020 Author: Sandeep K. Shinde Bench: Sandeep K. Shinde 906-Aba-397- 2020.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Ant. Bail Application No.397 Of 2020 Abdullah Hisamuddin Khan ... Applicant Vs The State of Maharashtra ... Respondents ... Mr. Tushar N. Sonawane for the Applicant. Mr. Y.M.Nakhwa , App for the Respondent-State.",
    "facts": "On 22nd January, 2020, three vehicles were intercepted at Kharegaon toll naka at Thane wherein the alleged gutkha products were found. One Mr. Sanket Sangle, co-accused had claimed ownership of the material found in the vehicles. It is the prosecution's case that applicant was to receive the delivery of the said goods. 4 It may be stated that except ofence punishable under Section 328 of the IPC, all ofences are bailable in nature.",
    "arguments": "The learned counsel for the applicant has relied upon the judgment in the case of Anand Ramdhani Chaurasia & Anr. v. State of Maharashtra & Ors. Dated 8th August, 2019 (in Writ Petition No.3607 of 2019)",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The learned counsel for the applicant has relied upon the judgment in the case of Anand Ramdhani Chaurasia & Anr. v. State of Maharashtra & Ors. Dated 8th August, 2019 (in Writ Petition No.3607 of 2019)",
